My goal is to build a literate program using noweb and C++. We are going to build an emulator for the Berzerk machine architecture of the Stern coin operated arcade game Berzerk. We will use the MAME emulator as the blueprint. Source code is at https://github.com/mamedev/mame
Mame has libraries of components (cpu's, vector generator/graphics chips, sound chips, TTL chips)
Each class of hardware has a driver. It is important in this project to accurately document and emulate the architecture of the original machine, and adhere to the design decisions that the MAME emulator team used as strictly as possible and to avoid inventing solutions to problems adhoc, no freehanding. 
We are going to develop a backend platform abstraction library for host graphics sound, video, window management and threading. We will only require one backend implementation. And for that we will need  the latest libsdl and associated libraries.
berzerk driver includes z80.cpp and other dependent components which will serve as blueprints for our own component library. 
Since arcade machine architectures generally involve multiple processors sharing memory, we want all memory access in emulated chips to be done via memory callbacks to ensure observability and provide means for instrumentation. 
https://github.com/mamedev/mame/blob/master/src/mame/stern/berzerk.cpp
