This emulator will one implementation of a common base class which will allow us to validate another implementation written in C++ without implementing the low level component emulation. It will be used to validate a C++ implementation of the this game using cosimulation, statistical measurement of events and unit tests. 
the berzerk disassembly is here: https://seanriddle.com/berzerk.asm we will be using this to meticulously document the subroutines and algorithms and data structures of the original game to sufficient degree that will enable us to implement the C++ version of the game in a bit accurate manner. We are going to build, debug and verify on a docker image with base image ubuntu 24. You will need latex to run noweb. Use cdoc directory to create markdown docs about our plans to document any bugs and solutions and todo tasks, features. Use noweb directory to generate the web files which will be tangled into C++ and woven into html and pdf.

Cosimulation goals:
The goal is to verify correctness at call return boundaries of side effects (register writes and memory writes and interrupts order agnostic, observable at call return). Note this assumes that magic RAM and sound are memory mapped IO which will later be replaced by higher level functional abstractions. 
In your plan.md what is currently Phase 6 (cosimulation) should be actually Phase 7. What should be phase 6 is a detailed documentation of subroutines, algorithms, data structures of the original game as represented in https://seanriddle.com/berzerk.asm to sufficient degree that will enable us to implement the C++ version of the game in a bit accurate and frame accurate manner.